{
  "title": "\u03c42-Bench: Evaluating Conversational Agents in a Dual-Control Environment",
  "authors": [
    "Victor Barres",
    "Honghua Dong",
    "Soham Ray",
    "Xujie Si",
    "Karthik Narasimhan"
  ],
  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2506.07982",
  "abstract": "\u03c42-Bench is a benchmark for conversational AI agents that simulates a dual-control environment, where both the agent and user can interact with the world using tools. This setup tests the agent's ability to communicate and collaborate with the user to solve tasks, and provides a more realistic scenario than traditional single-control benchmarks.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "Conversational AI agents need to be evaluated in environments where they can interact with users who have agency and can modify the state of the world. <strong>Dual-control environments</strong> provide a more realistic setting for testing these agents, as they require the agent to communicate and coordinate with the user to achieve a goal.",
      "visualization": {
        "type": "flow-diagram",
        "description": "A flow diagram showing the interaction between the agent and user in a dual-control environment, with the agent and user taking turns to use tools and communicate with each other.",
