          "title": "The Core Idea",
          "xLabel": "Steps",
          "yLabel": "Value"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The \u03c42-Bench benchmark uses a <strong>Decentralized Partially Observable Markov Decision Process (Dec-POMDP)</strong> to model the dual-control environment. The Dec-POMDP consists of two players, the agent and the user, who can communicate and use tools to interact with the environment. The benchmark also includes a <strong>compositional task generator</strong> that creates diverse and verifiable tasks from atomic components.",
      "visualization": {
        "type": "neural-network",
